{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789465828,"nonce":"tmF41sBNiO4yg5e6ynUUIJIDb8A=","title":"Cranelift's compile runs under the backend lock","message":"`ZyntaxCraneliftBackend::compile` holds the backend mutex from translation through `define_function` and `finalize_definitions`. A background promotion of `main` holds it for the whole compile, and a first-call compile on the main thread waits: a 17-instruction function took 11 ms to appear because a 680-instruction promotion held the lock (ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY=1 shows the wait as compile time with codegen at 0.27 ms).\n\nTranslation needs the module (declarations, data ids) and stays under the lock; Cranelift's `Context::compile(isa)` does not, and `JITModule::define_function_bytes` takes its output back under the lock. Split the compile into those three steps in the adapter, with the ISA held as an `Arc\u003cdyn TargetIsa\u003e` from construction. OSR helper compiles at tier 1 take the same path.","files":null}]}